            0.597,
            0.071,
            0.813,
            0.088
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Two Variables, One Line"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.841,
            0.071,
            0.881,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "113"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.11,
            0.852,
            0.13
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the following pairs of linear equations in two variables."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.134,
            0.471,
            0.153
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pair 1: 2x + y = 6 and x – y = 2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.157,
            0.485,
            0.176
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pair 2: x + y = 4 and 2x + 2y = 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.18,
            0.519,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pair 3: 3x – 2y = 6 and 6x – 4y = 12"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.204,
            0.495,
            0.224
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pair 4: x – 2y = 4 and 2x – 4y = 6"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.229,
            0.881,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "For each pair, prepare a table of values (with at least two ordered pairs). Plot the points on the Cartesian plane. Draw the straight lines."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.283,
            0.4,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.32,
            0.854,
            0.379
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How do we find solutions from the graph? What can we say about the number of solutions when the two lines (i) intersect at a point, (ii) are parallel, (iii) are coincident?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.392,
            0.879,
            0.43
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solutions to the pair of equations are points that lie on both lines. Thus"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.195,
            0.43,
            0.881,
            0.468
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) when the lines intersect in a single point, there is a unique solution;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.469,
            0.83,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) when the lines are parallel, there are no solutions; and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.183,
            0.489,
            0.881,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) when the lines are coincident, there are infinitely many solutions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.532,
            0.881,
            0.572
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 11:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Solve the pair of linear equations "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x + 3y = 6"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and 2x – 3y = 12 graphically. Comment on the nature of the solution."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.576,
            0.881,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider the equation x + 3y = 6. Expressing y in terms of x, we get "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = { \\frac { 6 - x } { 3 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.63,
            0.882,
            0.689
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Considering x to be first 0 and then 6 we obtain the corresponding values of y as 2 and 0 respectively. Hence (0, 2) and (6, 0) are points on the line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.367,
            0.689,
            0.631,
            0.754
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 17,
              "bbox": [
                0.367,
                0.689,
                0.631,
                0.754
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_28_table_17.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>x</td><td>0</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>y</td><td>2</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.761,
            0.883,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now consider the equation 2x – 3y = 12. Expressing y in terms of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " we "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{get}y = \\frac{2x - 12}{3}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . Considering x to be 0 and then 3, we obtain the values of y as –4, and –2 respectively. Hence (0, –4) and (3, –2) are points on the line."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.369,
            0.846,
            0.631,
            0.911
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
